# Generated registries produced by scripts/background/build-*.ts from the label archive.
#
# Build inputs stay out of version control: they are large, they are consumed only by other build
# scripts and tests, and the builders that produce them are versioned instead.
#
# The four registries the published corpus itself reads are the exception, and they are tracked
# below. `scripts/seed-data/background/index.ts` loads them at runtime, so a deploy without them
# publishes a corpus missing every record they carry — which is what happened: three of these were
# ignored, and the live site held a third of the records this repository could produce while every
# local check passed. A file the application reads ships with the application.
#
# Written as `data/registries/*` rather than `data/registries/`: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation under one never takes effect.
data/registries/*
!data/registries/substance-backed-background.json
!data/registries/compound-identity-background.json
!data/registries/supplement-background.json
!data/registries/label-presence.json
!data/registries/combination-row-composition.json
!data/registries/acquisition-cost.json
!data/registries/biological-identity.json
